syntax:
In a namespace:

namespace N {
    class A {
        friend void f(); // unqualified friend declaration
        friend class B; // friend class declaration
    };
}

Friend declaration inside class:

class C {
    friend void g(); // unqualified friend declaration
    friend class D; // friend class
};

Note: Friend functions and classes are not members of the class or namespace; they are granted access but do not affect lookup outside their declaration context.
